BUFSUM - sum the bytes of a buffer BASIC built with DIM + ?.

Language features
  - the memory bridge: DIM name size reserves a block, ? pokes bytes
  - passing a raw address to a seed
  - processing BASIC-owned memory at native speed

Try it
  DIM B% 9
    FOR I = 0 TO 9 : B%?I = I*I : NEXT
    SEED h%, "BUFSUM.SED" : PRINT CALL(h%, B%, 10)

Build it on the machine
  grow bufsum          # -> build/BUFSUM.SED
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as BUFSUM.SED, ready to use.

